   "text": "A sea shanty is a work song from the age of sail. A shantyman sang the lines and the crew answered with the chorus, pulling on the beat so that a dozen sailors hauled as one. Different jobs had different shanties: short-haul for quick tugs, halyard for hoisting sails, capstan for the slow walk round the winch, pumping for the bilges. They belong to merchant ships of the 1800s, and many were collected and written down by singers and folklorists in the following century.",
